; The ordinary-OCaml half of ppx_windtrap: generated code and the
; inline_tests backend's runner address it as
; Ppx_windtrap_runtime.Ppx_runtime — the wrapped library name is the
; spelling, so windtrap's internal module layout stays out of generated
; code. It consumes the core through Windtrap.Private's facades
; (windtrap_driver.mli is the census).
;
; windtrap_mutation is a link dependency, not an API edge: the inline
; runner is a thin driver, and the driver linking windtrap.mutation is
; what arms mutation (see lib/mutation/dune). No module here names the
; loop — the loop installs itself into the core's Registry at module
; load, and its -linkall archive is what guarantees the unit loads —
; so this line is what carries it into every generated runner's
; closure, exactly the linking a test stanza's explicit
; windtrap.mutation entry provides for the standalone runner. Without
; it an inline mutation run would silently fall back to a plain run
; (test/mutate_loop/inline is the fence).

(library
 (name ppx_windtrap_runtime)
 (public_name ppx_windtrap.runtime)
 (libraries windtrap windtrap_mutation)
 ; The core measures its own coverage, and Ppx_runtime moved out of it;
 ; keeping the backend keeps the measured set intact. No mutation
 ; stanza, deliberately: the runtime is part of the machinery that
 ; judges mutants, and a mutant armed inside the judging process hangs
 ; — ppx_runtime.ml's [@@@mutate exclude_file] states the same intent
 ; in-file. Inert without --instrument-with.
 (instrumentation
  (backend ppx_windtrap.coverage)))
